@startuml AuthorMe

title Me API Sequence

' Leading SQL apostrophes use &#39; so PlantUML preserves literals; parity compares decoded SQL.

' Visual style
skinparam defaultFontName "Sarabun"
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #475569
    ArrowFontColor #334155
    LifeLineBorderColor #CBD5E1
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    ParticipantBorderColor #94A3B8
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
    ParticipantFontColor #0F172A
    GroupBorderColor #94A3B8
    GroupBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    GroupFontColor #334155
}

' Do not show participant footers at the bottom of the diagram
hide footbox
actor "User" as user
box "Frontend" #F8FAFC
    participant "Me Page" as page
end box
box "Web API" #F8FAFC
    participant "API" as api
    participant "Application" as app
    participant "Domain" as domain
    participant "Infrastructure" as infra
end box
box "Database" #F8FAFC
    database "t_user_access_token" as t_user_access_token
end box
user -> page: Request own effective token roles
activate page
page -> api: GET v1/author/me (Bearer JWT, timestamp, requestId)
activate api
api -> app: [**MeQueryHandler**] Process request
activate app
app -> app: Generate requestId if omitted; validate mandatory UTC timestamp
note over app, infra
    Validate mandatory timestamp as a UTC timestamp before SQL; missing/malformed timestamp returns 400 E10001.
    Generate requestId if omitted. Missing/malformed Bearer credentials or a failed JWT
    signature/issuer/audience/expiry/sub/role-claim validation return the same 401 E10002 `Invalid or expired
    access token.` before SQL.
    Validate the `roles` claim of the payload defined by
    [login](../../authen-and-author/02-login/spec.md#claim-resolution-and-payload) (owner-confirmed 2026-11-13):
    roles must be an array of unique non-empty strings, including explicit [] for no roles. Missing/non-array
    roles, non-string or duplicate entries make the credential invalid (401); never silently replace malformed
    claims with an empty list or recover privileges from the database. The other claims (`user`, `permissions`,
    `scopes`) are not used and are not response fields.
end note
alt Missing or malformed timestamp
    app -> api: HTTP 400 E10001
    api -> page: Header validation error
else Valid ordinary headers
    app -> app: Verify JWT signature/issuer/audience/exp/UUID sub and roles claim as unique non-empty strings (payload of 2026-11-13)
    alt Missing/invalid JWT or malformed roles claim
        app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
        api -> page: Authentication error
    else Verified JWT and roles array
        app -> app: userId = verified sub; accessTokenHash = SHA-256 exact JWT
        alt Read-only processing completes
            app -> app: Capture fresh server UTC now before credential query; recheck JWT exp
            app -> infra: QUERY - Check active credential and user
            infra -> t_user_access_token: QUERY - Check active credential and user
            activate t_user_access_token
                note right of t_user_access_token
                    SELECT
                        at.user_id
                    FROM authen.t_user_access_token at
                    WHERE at.token = '<sequence.accessTokenHash>'
                    AND at.user_id = '<sequence.userId>'
                    AND at.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                    AND at.expired_at > '<sequence.now>'
                    AND EXISTS (
                        SELECT 1
                        FROM authen.m_user u
                        WHERE u.id = at.user_id
                        AND u.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                    )
                end note
                t_user_access_token -> infra: Return ACTIVE matching token/user or no row
            deactivate t_user_access_token
            infra -> app: Return ACTIVE matching token/user or no row
            alt Credential/user ACTIVE and stored/JWT expiry valid at now
                app -> app: roles = copy the role names from verifiedJwt.roles; sort ordinal
                alt Token roles is empty
                    app -> app: data.roles = []; isPlatformAdmin = false
                else Returned token roles contain exact name PLATFORM_ADMIN
                    app -> app: data.roles = sorted token roles; isPlatformAdmin = true
                else Other token roles
                    app -> app: data.roles = sorted token roles; isPlatformAdmin = false
                end
                app -> app: data.userId = verified sub; ignore independent admin flag; no live role-table lookup
                note over app, infra
                    This detailed endpoint revision remains in-review; no backend implementation is included. Any caller with a
                    valid access token can call this API, and sees only the caller's own snapshot.
                    Capture fresh server UTC now immediately before the one credential query and recheck JWT expiry at now. The
                    query must find the ACTIVE, unexpired stored token for that hash/userId and an ACTIVE user.
                    Missing/revoked/expired token, mismatched owner or inactive user returns the same 401. No request userId,
                    role, role name or isPlatformAdmin value controls this lookup or the response.
                    Do not query author.t_user_role or author.m_role to reload, filter, rename or replace those roles.
                    Role/assignment changes after issuance do not change this token's response; an old PLATFORM_ADMIN token may
                    still report true until its own expiry, exactly as its privileges remain usable under Q4. The current
                    token/user status check still allows logout/password reset to revoke credentials immediately (Q13).
                    Copy the role names from the verified roles; sort them using ordinal case-sensitive comparison.
                    isPlatformAdmin is true exactly when one returned role name equals PLATFORM_ADMIN (case-sensitive). Do not
                    trust an independent isPlatformAdmin token claim or a request flag. roles=[] returns isPlatformAdmin=false.
                    Database rows are not needed to sort or compute this flag. Because the new payload carries role names only,
                    `data.roles` is an array of role-name strings and no longer returns `roleId` (decided by the SA, pending
                    confirmation).
                    Every refresh resolves latest ACTIVE grants for the newly issued token. Calling this endpoint with that
                    refreshed token reports the refreshed snapshot, while an older still-valid token keeps its own prior roles.
                    The endpoint never refreshes a token or alters role assignments itself. Current profile/lifecycle data is
                    not substituted for role claims.
                    Response: data.userId, data.isPlatformAdmin and data.roles, an array of role-name strings only. Permissions
                    and scopes are not returned by this endpoint even though login/refresh carry them; no permission grant is
                    inferred from the response. Never return stored token hashes or internal credential ids.
                    After valid input/JWT, perform the single credential query, then map the snapshot and return 200 S10000.
                    There is no 403 for a non-admin or no-role token. Timeout returns 408 E90001; unexpected failure returns
                    generic 500 with no new bizCode. No outcome writes data and no 200 is sent before credential validation and
                    snapshot mapping complete.
                end note
                app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 Inquiry Me Success; data.userId, data.isPlatformAdmin, data.roles
                api -> page: Return calling-token role snapshot
                page -> user: Display privileges of this token
            else Credential/user inactive, revoked, mismatched or expired
                app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
                api -> page: Authentication error
            end
        else Timeout during read-only processing
            app -> api: HTTP 408 E90001
            api -> page: Inquiry timed out; no writes
        else Unexpected read-only failure
            app -> api: HTTP 500 Internal Server Error; omit bizCode
            api -> page: Generic inquiry failure; no writes
        end
    end
end
deactivate app
deactivate api
deactivate page
@enduml
